# Cross-routes cohort (issue #504).
# First Linux cross-build cohort, not a mandate to build every target
# from every host. Native rows qualified under issues #410-#414; Linux
# same-arch musl closures qualified under issue #411; Linux cross-arch
# rows stay in the first cohort with separate native target execution
# plus separate cache and remote evidence. Optional macOS expansion only
# if bounded upstream configuration suffices. Excluded routes are outside
# the initial qualification cohort, not claims of impossibility.
# All-cross mandate rejected; native only with no Windows/macOS cross-host claim.

exec: Linux x86_64 -> Linux x86_64 and arm64, each glibc and static musl
exec: Linux x86_64 -> First Linux cross-build cohort
exec: Linux x86_64 -> x86_64 static musl qualified under issue #411 on ubuntu-latest with bazel-musl-x86_64- scope
exec: Linux arm64 -> Linux arm64 and x86_64, each glibc and static musl
exec: Linux arm64 -> Native arm64 glibc qualified under issue #410 on ubuntu-24.04-arm with bazel-arm64- scope
exec: Linux arm64 -> arm64 static musl qualified under issue #411 on ubuntu-24.04-arm with bazel-musl-arm64- scope
exec: Linux arm64 -> arm64-to-x86_64 cross stays in the first Linux cross-build cohort
target: Linux x86_64 glibc
target: Linux arm64 glibc
target: Linux x86_64 static musl
target: Linux arm64 static musl
target: Linux x86_64-to-arm64 glibc plus static musl
target: Linux arm64-to-x86_64 glibc plus static musl
native: Native x86_64 glibc qualified under issue #410 on ubuntu-latest seed
native: Native arm64 glibc qualified under issue #410 on ubuntu-24.04-arm with bazel-arm64- scope
native: Native macOS arm64 qualified under issue #412 on macos-14 with bazel-macos-arm64- scope
native: Native macOS x86_64 best-effort qualified under issue #413 on macos-15-intel with bazel-macos-x86_64- scope
native: Native Windows x86_64 qualified under issue #414 on windows-latest with bazel-windows-x86_64- scope
expansion: macOS arm64 -> Linux x86_64 and arm64 profiles, then macOS x86_64
expansion: Optional first expansion if bounded upstream configuration suffices
expansion: Expand only after the initial cohort passes
excluded: Linux-to-Windows outside the initial qualification cohort, not claims of impossibility
excluded: macOS-to-Windows outside the initial qualification cohort, not claims of impossibility
excluded: Linux-to-macOS outside the initial qualification cohort, not claims of impossibility
excluded: Windows-to-macOS outside the initial qualification cohort, not claims of impossibility
excluded: Windows-to-Linux outside the initial qualification cohort, not claims of impossibility
excluded: Windows arm64 outside the initial qualification cohort, not claims of impossibility
excluded: do not require Linux/macOS-to-Windows, Linux/Windows-to-macOS, Windows-to-Linux, or Windows arm64 to complete this cohort
rejected: all-cross mandate
rejected: every target from every host
scope: Native only with glibc plus static musl on Linux x86_64 and arm64
scope: dynamic musl explicitly out of scope
scope: no Windows or macOS cross-host claim
